    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d569-a1">

                <pb facs="0646" n="388" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg388"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Statement for the press</hi><anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d569-f1"/>
                </head>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Payments of Freight on detained Cargoes in Great
                        Britain</hi>
                </p>
                <p>Shippers of freight in German or Austro-Hungarian vessels which cleared from the
                    United States before the war, and were captured or detained in British ports,
                    are informed that, in case they have paid freight in order to secure the release
                    of their goods, they should at once make claim for its reimbursement. <pb
                        facs="0647" n="389" xml:id="pg389"/> Claims of this character should be
                    supported by proofs of the payments in question and may be transmitted to the
                    American Consul General at London who will submit them to the proper officer of
                    the prize court, or they may be submitted through the solicitors originally
                    employed to bring about the release.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
